module gunbc.machine_intake.mtcollins1_virtual_media_readout_observation

// MTCOLLINS1 PHASE B0 (gunbc.plans.boot_origin_bmc_media B0; discharges work item
// adhoc-9e4ea90a-fd0 alongside adhoc-b4222c87-d37): WHAT THE CONTROLLER ADMITS FOR VIRTUAL MEDIA,
// AND WHAT COULD NOT BE READ.
//
// The B0 reading is the field `admitted_protocols` of a RedfishVirtualMediaProbeReceipt
// (extdeps.bmc.redfish_virtual_media). The boot lane's media-route selector consumes exactly that
// field: an admitted protocol selects the route, an EMPTY admitted list is refused as
// CandidateRedfishProbeEmpty, and a contradictory one as CandidateRedfishProbeContradictory
// (gunbc.boot_artifact_delivery redfish_eligibility). No receipt and no reading is the third
// state -- and that is what this phase produced.
//
// WHY THE PLAN'S OWN PREMISE HAD TO BE CORRECTED FIRST. The plan text (boot_origin_bmc_media
// line 30), and the planning lanes that repeat it, state that mtcollins1 "serves no Redfish",
// citing gunbc.machine_intake.mtcollins1_access_observation, whose Redfish rows were taken on
// 2026-09-11 under firmware 0.32. That premise is no longer true and it is load-bearing, so it is
// corrected by measurement rather than by argument. On 2026-10-27T00:54:24Z, against the SAME
// address (192.168.1.228:443) on the 0.45 build, the controller answers:
//
//   GET /redfish/v1/                             200   Server: AMI MegaRAC Redfish Service
//   GET /redfish/v1/Managers/Self/VirtualMedia   401   WWW-Authenticate: Basic, X-Auth-Token
//
// The service root is served with its full DMTF body -- RedfishVersion 1.5.0, @odata.id
// /redfish/v1/, Id "RootService", and the Links roster (AccountService, Chassis, Managers,
// Registries, SessionService, Sessions, Systems, UpdateService, JsonSchemas). Under 0.32 the
// identical ladder returned 404 at every /redfish path while the web root served 200
// (mtcollins1_access_observation, the mtcollins1_http_probes rows). So "no Redfish" was a property
// of the 0.32 firmware, not of the box, and the reflash to 0.45 brought a Redfish service with it.
// The observation below is the record of that, made on the controller rather than inherited from
// the plan. It does NOT touch mtcollins1_access_observation, which remains the true record of what
// was observed on 2026-09-11 under 0.32: correcting a stale CONCLUSION by editing a dated
// OBSERVATION would destroy the older measurement that is still evidence.
//
// IDENTITY, BECAUSE A SURFACE READ AT AN ADDRESS IS NOT YET A READ OF A UNIT. The 0.32 intake row
// established the address-MAC-FRU join; this read adds the one leg that ties THIS answer to that
// unit without any credential: the served service root carries
// UUID "d5b80e46-903a-1000-01e6-4cd68a3cc128", and its last 12 hex digits are the controller's own
// MAC, nibble-reversed -- MAC 28:C1:3C:8A:D6:4C read backwards is 4c:d6:8a:3c:c1:28. That MAC is
// the one recorded on the FRU's Board Extra field ("28C13C8AD64C" in the committed intake capture)
// and the one the operator's static reservation bmc-mtcollins1 binds; that UUID is the one the
// host reports from its own SMBIOS tables. Reproducing the unit's burned UUID and MAC is not
// something an answer-on-the-IP can do, so the address, the served Redfish service and the unit
// are the same box.
//
// WHAT B0 CANNOT SETTLE, AND WHY IT IS NOT PAVED OVER. TransferProtocolType allowable values live
// inside the VirtualMedia resource bodies. Those bodies are NOT in the unauthenticated surface:
// every Redfish collection and resource path, and the OEM /api/settings/media/general path, answer
// 401 Unauthorized with Basic and X-Auth-Token challenges. The reading that could fill
// admitted_protocols must be AUTHENTICATED, and the read-only BMC credential is unreachable from
// the observation lane: its Secret Manager container is dispatched from the fleet-converge
// runner's own identity (extdeps.cloud.gcp.secret_manager secret_version_payload_read), and this
// observing container has no ADC, no workload-identity federation and no grant. That is the typed
// gap below. It is a gap in the CREDENTIAL, not in the SURFACE -- which is precisely the
// distinction the surface premise got wrong, so both halves are carried in one receipt.
//
// THE AUTHENTICATED AXIS IS ALSO MEASURED, NOT ASSUMED. It is not the case that "the account
// works, we simply did not present it". The boot lane HAS presented a credential to these
// resources on the 0.45 build and been refused: boot runs 40258937016 and 40264233543 each carry
// the line "redfish: UNREAD: BMC refused the credential at
// https://192.168.1.228/redfish/v1/Systems (2026-10-25T12:02:34Z, exit 22): curl: (22) The
// requested URL returned error: 401", from captures whose SHA256 digests are pinned below. So the
// authenticated read of VirtualMedia is not merely unattempted here; its closest available proxy
// in the corpus is a refusal. That is a reason to expect the authenticated read to need work (the
// health reader does not exist on this box yet), not a reason to guess its answer.
//
// THEREFORE B0 SELECTS NEITHER ROUTE. The B0 rule is "DirectRedfishHttps when HTTPS is listed,
// NfsRelayThroughHolder otherwise, an unread value selects neither". `admitted_protocols` is
// unread: no reader in this corpus has ever received the member bodies that carry it. So it is
// neither EMPTY -- which would be a read that admitted nothing -- nor populated. B0's third arm
// fires: neither route is selected, and B3 (the NFS relay) is NOT built on this reading's
// authority. The deciding read is named exactly, because "unread" without a named next read is how
// a phase stays unread forever: an authenticated GET of the VirtualMedia collection and its
// members as the health-ReadOnly principal (gunbc.bmc.bmc_health_reader, username gunbc_health) --
// NOT as bmc-mtcollins1-gunbc v2, which is the boot/operator credential and the wrong principal
// for a GET. The read-only pattern to copy is gunbc.fleet.fleet_health_observe, whose every arm is
// a GET on redfish.Http authenticated through a private per-run netrc shredded on every path out.
//
// A CAUTION THIS RECEIPT CANNOT LIFT, INHERITED FROM ITS ADDRESS. A firmware reflash restores
// factory accounts and erases the remote-media configuration, so a 401 seen while or after a
// firmware converge can say nothing about the endpoint (gunbc.recurring_failure_mode
// .firmware_reflash_resets_the_bmc_credential_it_needs). Checked the same hour: no mtcollins
// firmware-converge run was in flight (the latest fleet-converge runs completed at 2026-10-26
// T14:12Z, 21:05Z and 22:32Z, all before this probe), so the 401 rows here are not confounded by a
// reflash in progress. mtcollins1 is also the standing boot target of
// gunbc.fleet.mtcollins_firmware_converge, so a boot may present media concurrently: read this as
// a snapshot of the SURFACE, never as a settled media state.
//
// PROVENANCE. Out-of-band only. Every request was an HTTPS GET issued from the observer's network
// position; nothing was written, no session created, no account touched, no media action sent, and
// no credential was fetched or presented. In-band ipmitool was not used as a fallback (operator
// ruling 2026-09-18: fleet observation is out-of-band and least-privilege). Raw captures, with
// their SHA256SUMS, are committed beside this module at
// artifacts/bmc/mtcollins1-virtual-media-readonly-probe-192.168.1.228-20261027T005424Z/, and the
// digests below are those files' digests: re-reading them re-derives every row here.

import std.types { Bool, Int, NonEmptyStr, List, EpochMs, list_length }
import std.optional { Present, Absent }
import std.list { list_member, first_where }
import std.content_hash { ContentHash, Sha256Digest, Sha256Hash }
import extdeps.bmc.endpoint { BmcControllerEndpoint }
import extdeps.bmc.capability { BmcFirmwareReleaseIdentity }
import extdeps.bmc.access_profile {
  BmcAccessSurface,
  BmcObservedIdentity,
  SurfaceOemRestRemoteMedia,
  SurfaceRedfishVirtualMedia,
  SurfaceSystemInventory,
}
import extdeps.bmc.redfish_virtual_media {
  RedfishVirtualMediaLocator,
  UnderManager,
  UnderSystem,
  RedfishVirtualMediaTransferProtocol,
  TransferHttps,
}
import gunbc.machine_intake.mtcollins1_access_observation {
  mtcollins1_endpoint,
  mtcollins1_identity,
}
import gunbc.host.bmc_release_capability_catalog { megarac_committed_hpm_check_identity }

// THE B0 DECISION, AS A VALUE. The plan's three arms become three constructors so that "unread" is
// a case every consumer must handle, rather than a default that can silently look like a decision.
type BmcMediaRouteAdmission
  = DirectRedfishHttps
  | NfsRelayThroughHolder
  | RouteUnsettledUnread { cause: NonEmptyStr }

// WHETHER A READ ACTUALLY EXPOSED THE TRANSFER PROTOCOLS. Three states, because the corpus already
// holds two of them and they mean different things downstream: a receipt whose list is EMPTY says
// the controller ANSWERED and admitted nothing (gunbc.boot_artifact_delivery refuses that as
// CandidateRedfishProbeEmpty), while a receipt never obtained says nobody has ever seen the field.
// Collapsing the second into the first would let an absent read masquerade as a settled refusal --
// and a settled refusal is exactly what would be cited to authorize building the NFS relay.
type TransferProtocolReadout
  = ReadoutRead { protocols: List<RedfishVirtualMediaTransferProtocol> }
  | ReadoutRefusedUnauthenticated { challenge: NonEmptyStr }
  | ReadoutNeverAttempted

// ONE ROW OF THE STATUS LADDER. `method` is carried rather than implied so this record cannot hold
// a write while presenting itself as what was issued: this phase sent GETs, and the witness counts
// the rows over it.
type BmcSurfaceProbeRow {
  method: NonEmptyStr
  path: NonEmptyStr
  status: Int
}

// THE B0 RECEIPT, AS THIS PHASE ACTUALLY MET IT.
type B0VirtualMediaReadout {
  endpoint: BmcControllerEndpoint
  // What the controller reports itself to be, taken from the boot lane's committed 0.45 hpm check
  // -- the same identity mtcollins1_current_build_firmware carries. The 0.32 intake row is NOT
  // reused: 0.32 is the firmware whose ladder produced "no Redfish", and labelling a 0.45 surface
  // read with 0.32 would misdate the entire observation.
  firmware: BmcFirmwareReleaseIdentity?
  identity: BmcObservedIdentity
  // The unauthenticated ladder, one row per path, in the order issued. The ladder IS the finding:
  // 200 at the service root, 401 at everything below it.
  ladder: List<BmcSurfaceProbeRow>
  transfer_protocol_readout: TransferProtocolReadout
  // Both cited collection locations, listed rather than guessed, because which one an endpoint
  // serves is itself per-endpoint discovery and an unauthenticated ladder cannot settle it:
  // Managers/Self (where mtjade1, another MegaRAC, is known to publish it) and Systems/1 (the
  // older location the schema still allows).
  candidate_locators: List<RedfishVirtualMediaLocator>
  // True when the service root itself was served -- the fact that retires "serves no Redfish" for
  // this firmware, independently of any credential.
  redfish_service_root_served: Bool
  // Which authentication mechanisms the controller offered for the refused VirtualMedia GET.
  offered_auth_schemes: List<NonEmptyStr>
  credential_path_available: Bool
  credential_principal: NonEmptyStr
  // Whether a firmware converge was live against this unit when the ladder was taken: the check
  // that keeps a 401 from being read as a property of the surface.
  firmware_converge_live_at_observation: Bool
  observed_at: EpochMs
  discovered_surfaces: List<BmcAccessSurface>
  raw_capture_digest: ContentHash
  // Digests of the boot-lane captures that carry the authenticated 401 rows, so the authenticated
  // axis of this receipt is checkable against artifacts/bmc/ rather than against prose.
  authenticated_refusal_captures: List<ContentHash>
}

fn probe_row(path: NonEmptyStr, status: Int) -> BmcSurfaceProbeRow {
  BmcSurfaceProbeRow { method: "GET", path: path, status: status }
}

// 2026-10-27T00:54:24Z. Reproduced row-for-row from the committed surface-ladder.txt.
data b0_ladder: List<BmcSurfaceProbeRow> = [
  probe_row(path: "/redfish", status: 401),
  probe_row(path: "/redfish/v1", status: 401),
  probe_row(path: "/redfish/v1/", status: 200),
  probe_row(path: "/redfish/v1/Systems", status: 401),
  probe_row(path: "/redfish/v1/Managers", status: 401),
  probe_row(path: "/redfish/v1/Managers/Self", status: 401),
  probe_row(path: "/redfish/v1/Managers/Self/VirtualMedia", status: 401),
  probe_row(path: "/redfish/v1/Systems/1", status: 401),
  probe_row(path: "/redfish/v1/Systems/1/VirtualMedia", status: 401),
  probe_row(path: "/redfish/v1/Chassis", status: 401),
  probe_row(path: "/redfish/v1/SessionService", status: 401),
  probe_row(path: "/redfish/v1/AccountService", status: 401),
  probe_row(path: "/api/session", status: 404),
  probe_row(path: "/api/settings/media/general", status: 401),
  probe_row(path: "/", status: 200),
]

// THE 401 CHALLENGE AS THE CONTROLLER RENDERED IT, split into the two schemes it will accept for a
// VirtualMedia GET. Realm names only: no credential, token or cookie value appears here or in the
// captures (the committed header files carry no Authorization and no Set-Cookie line).
data b0_offered_auth_schemes: List<NonEmptyStr> = ["Basic", "X-Auth-Token"]

data b0_unauthenticated_challenge: NonEmptyStr =
  "Basic realm=\"AMI_Redfish_Server\", X-Auth-Token realm=\"AMI_Redfish_Server\""

// THE TWO CITED COLLECTION LOCATIONS, with media_id "CD" as the one named member to read first.
// Neither is claimed to be THE location this controller uses; that answer comes back with the
// member bodies. The media_id is a starting point for the authenticated read, not a claim that a
// "CD" member exists.
data b0_candidate_locators: List<RedfishVirtualMediaLocator> = [
  RedfishVirtualMediaLocator { parent: UnderManager { manager_id: "Self" }, media_id: "CD" },
  RedfishVirtualMediaLocator { parent: UnderSystem { system_id: "1" }, media_id: "CD" },
]

// THE CREDENTIAL AXIS, STATED AS A GAP WITH ITS PRINCIPAL NAMED. The read that fills
// admitted_protocols authenticates as the health-ReadOnly account (gunbc.bmc.bmc_health_reader,
// username gunbc_health, container "bmc-<host>-health-reader"), never as bmc-mtcollins1-gunbc v2:
// that is the boot/operator credential, and presenting an operator principal to make a read-only
// observation would silently promote it into an observation lane. The health reader is not yet
// provisioned for mtcollins1 -- no bmc-mtcollins1-health-reader container is rostered in
// gunbc.secret_provision -- and the observation lane holds no Secret Manager grant at all, so
// NEITHER credential is reachable from here. That is why the gap is reported instead of being
// worked around with the nearest credential to hand.
data b0_credential_principal: NonEmptyStr =
  "gunbc_health (Redfish ReadOnly, gunbc.bmc.bmc_health_reader); not provisioned for mtcollins1; bmc-mtcollins1-gunbc v2 is the boot credential and is not the principal for this read"

// THE B0 READING ITSELF.
data mtcollins1_b0_virtual_media_readout: B0VirtualMediaReadout = B0VirtualMediaReadout {
  endpoint: mtcollins1_endpoint,
  firmware: megarac_committed_hpm_check_identity,
  identity: mtcollins1_identity,
  ladder: b0_ladder,
  // UNREAD. Not an empty list, and not a refusal that may be read as a "no": no reader has ever
  // received the member bodies that carry the field.
  transfer_protocol_readout: ReadoutRefusedUnauthenticated { challenge: b0_unauthenticated_challenge },
  candidate_locators: b0_candidate_locators,
  // TRUE, and the load-bearing half of the correction.
  redfish_service_root_served: true,
  offered_auth_schemes: b0_offered_auth_schemes,
  credential_path_available: false,
  credential_principal: b0_credential_principal,
  firmware_converge_live_at_observation: false,
  // 2026-10-27T00:54:24Z.
  observed_at: 1793062464000,
  // DISCOVERED, not confirmed: something answers behind authentication at the Redfish inventory
  // paths and at the OEM media-settings path. Neither is a confirmed success, because no
  // authenticated GET has completed. That distinction keeps this receipt from being mistaken for
  // the access observation it sits beside, whose successful_read_surfaces ARE confirmed reads.
  discovered_surfaces: [SurfaceSystemInventory, SurfaceRedfishVirtualMedia, SurfaceOemRestRemoteMedia],
  // sha256 over the committed SHA256SUMS manifest of the capture directory, which itself covers
  // every file in it: ARGV.txt, META.txt, surface-ladder.txt, redfish_ServiceRoot.json,
  // redfish_ServiceRoot_headers.txt, redfish_VirtualMedia_401_headers.txt.
  raw_capture_digest: Sha256Hash(Sha256Digest { hex: "8b1de691e5126769f914313108f16605f29325bc797d62a491265525118a7800" }),
  // mtcollins1-boot-run-40258937016 and -40264233543, mtcollins1-boot-diagnostics.txt, digests of
  // the committed files as they stand.
  authenticated_refusal_captures: [
    Sha256Hash(Sha256Digest { hex: "16a18fed0a9630d33194fef1a0a5efb80807f64b2363ad7e63f94cc44dec498f" }),
    Sha256Hash(Sha256Digest { hex: "e419f3fcc65dea77b6774ae037067c82a03acf3e3784ea4ef5f63be8d41b2822" }),
  ],
}

fn protocol_eq(a: RedfishVirtualMediaTransferProtocol, b: RedfishVirtualMediaTransferProtocol) -> Bool {
  a == b
}

fn protocol_in(xs: List<RedfishVirtualMediaTransferProtocol>, x: RedfishVirtualMediaTransferProtocol) -> Bool {
  list_member(xs: xs, x: x, eq: protocol_eq)
}

// THE SELECTOR'S RULES AS PREDICATES, because this substrate has no list filter: the ladder is
// asked questions through folds, and the witness uses the same doors rather than re-implementing
// them, so a wrong door fails both sides at once.
fn ladder_status(readout: B0VirtualMediaReadout, path: NonEmptyStr) -> Int {
  match first_where(readout.ladder, r => r.path == path) {
    Present { value: row } => row.status
    Absent => -1
  }
}

fn ladder_is_get_only(readout: B0VirtualMediaReadout) -> Bool {
  readout.ladder.all(r => r.method == "GET")
}

// B0'S RULE, AS A FUNCTION THE NEXT PHASE MUST MATCH ON -- the operator's ruling of 2026-09-18,
// re-confirmed on this task, rendered one arm per sentence:
//
//   "A read that returns the allowable list with HTTPS in it selects DirectRedfishHttps. A read
//    that returns non-HTTPS protocols (NFS-only, or any other non-HTTPS set) selects
//    NfsRelayThroughHolder. Only a read where no protocol has been admitted at all, or a refusal,
//    selects neither route."
//
// WHY THE MIDDLE ARM IS WIDER THAN THE PLAN'S SENTENCE SOUNDS. Only the direct route needs the
// controller itself to admit HTTPS, because the relay feeds the share through the holder and the
// controller attaches it over the OEM remote-media path, which takes NFS or CIFS shares without any
// Redfish TransferProtocolType admission. So "read, and not HTTPS" genuinely is "use the relay": a
// CIFS-only or SFTP-only answer is a reason to relay, not a reason to stop. HTTPS is tested FIRST,
// so the direct route wins when both are admitted -- preference belongs to the selector, not to the
// wire order.
//
// THE ARM THAT MUST NEVER FALL THROUGH. A refusal, a never-attempted reading, and a list with
// NOTHING admitted all select NEITHER route. The first two are the absence of an answer; the third
// is an answer that admitted nothing, which is not an admission of NFS either. Treating any of them
// as "not HTTPS, therefore relay" would build relay infrastructure on a read that never happened --
// the failure this phase exists to make unwritable, and what the witness drives hardest.
//
// THE EMPTY LIST IS THE ONE CASE WHERE THIS SELECTOR AND THE BOOT LANE'S OWN FOLD APART, and the
// divergence is deliberate rather than accidental. gunbc.boot_artifact_delivery redfish_eligibility
// files an empty receipt as CandidateRedfishProbeEmpty, because that fold asks "may this candidate
// be fetched over Redfish" and an empty admission answers no. This selector asks the plan's own
// question, "which media route do we take", and the ruling answers it with NEITHER for an empty
// list: admitting nothing is not an admission of NFS. Same receipt, two questions, no contradiction
// -- recorded here so the next reader does not "fix" one to match the other.
fn b0_media_route_admission(readout: B0VirtualMediaReadout) -> BmcMediaRouteAdmission {
  match readout.transfer_protocol_readout {
    ReadoutRead { protocols: protocols } =>
      if list_length(items: protocols) == 0 {
        RouteUnsettledUnread {
          cause: "VirtualMedia answered and admitted no protocol at all: nothing was admitted, which is not an admission of NFS and so selects neither route",
        }
      } else if protocol_in(xs: protocols, x: TransferHttps) {
        DirectRedfishHttps
      } else {
        NfsRelayThroughHolder
      }
    ReadoutRefusedUnauthenticated { challenge: challenge } => RouteUnsettledUnread {
      cause: concat(
        "VirtualMedia resource bodies are not in the unauthenticated surface: every collection path answered 401 (",
        concat(challenge, "); the TransferProtocolType allowable values have never been returned to any reader"),
      ),
    }
    ReadoutNeverAttempted => RouteUnsettledUnread {
      cause: "no VirtualMedia read has been attempted against this endpoint",
    }
  }
}

// B0'S RESULT, FOR CONSUMERS THAT SHOULD NOT RE-DERIVE IT. This is the datum the plan's B0 step
// exists to produce, and it says NEITHER ROUTE.
data mtcollins1_b0_media_route: BmcMediaRouteAdmission =
  b0_media_route_admission(readout: mtcollins1_b0_virtual_media_readout)

// THE GAP, TYPED -- because a gap that is a value can be gated on and a gap that is a comment
// cannot.
type B0CredentialGap
  = GapNone
  | GapCredentialUnreachable { principal: NonEmptyStr, cause: NonEmptyStr }

fn b0_credential_gap(readout: B0VirtualMediaReadout) -> B0CredentialGap {
  if readout.credential_path_available {
    GapNone
  } else {
    GapCredentialUnreachable {
      principal: readout.credential_principal,
      cause: "read-only credential unreachable from the observation lane: its Secret Manager container is dispatched only from the fleet-converge runner identity, and this container has no ADC, no workload-identity federation and no grant",
    }
  }
}

data mtcollins1_b0_credential_gap: B0CredentialGap =
  b0_credential_gap(readout: mtcollins1_b0_virtual_media_readout)

// WHETHER THE SURFACE PREMISE STILL HOLDS, AS A PREDICATE RATHER THAN A SENTENCE. It held while the
// 0.32-era reading stood; this reading makes it false, so any lane still asserting it is planning
// against a firmware that is no longer on the box.
fn b0_serves_no_redfish_premise_still_holds(readout: B0VirtualMediaReadout) -> Bool {
  !readout.redfish_service_root_served
}

// THE CHALLENGE TEXT, EXPOSED FOR THE WITNESS: a refusal receipt that does not carry what the
// controller offered is not usable by whoever resumes the read.
fn b0_challenge_of(readout: B0VirtualMediaReadout) -> NonEmptyStr {
  match readout.transfer_protocol_readout {
    ReadoutRefusedUnauthenticated { challenge: challenge } => challenge
    ReadoutRead { protocols: _ } => "read"
    ReadoutNeverAttempted => "never attempted"
  }
}

// THE CAUSE TEXT, EXPOSED FOR THE WITNESS for the same reason: the arms must be separable by their
// stated reasons, not only by their constructor names.
fn b0_route_cause(route: BmcMediaRouteAdmission) -> NonEmptyStr {
  match route {
    RouteUnsettledUnread { cause: cause } => cause
    DirectRedfishHttps => "direct-redfish-https"
    NfsRelayThroughHolder => "nfs-relay-through-holder"
  }
}

fn route_is_unsettled(route: BmcMediaRouteAdmission) -> Bool {
  match route {
    RouteUnsettledUnread { cause: _ } => true
    _ => false
  }
}

// THE ONE-LINE ANSWER B0 OWES THE PLAN: the Redfish service EXISTS on 0.45 (contrary to the 0.32
// premise the plan carries), TransferProtocolType is UNREAD, the deciding read is an authenticated
// GET by the health-ReadOnly principal (not provisioned for this unit), and therefore B3 is NOT
// authorized by this reading.
